    "body": "<img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24731903/147854851-f9322f70-4e48-45ac-ae93-2ea29ffa0a28.png\" alt=\"image\" width=\"200\" style=\"max-width: 100%\">\r\n\r\n`get_module` used to call `modules::handle` but the handling for `custom`/`env_var` is only in `handle_prompt`, which caused tests using `ModuleRenderer` to fail. So I made a hack to have it go through `handle_prompt` but there might be a cleaner way.\r\n\r\nChanging it here might also make it work with the `module` subcommand.\r\n\r\nBut still, this feels like a hack... With the whole recursion thing going on and the join...",
